sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-04> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Because ion channels open and close post-translationally, the same channels can yield different voltage states depending on cell history and different channels can yield the same voltage map, the information content of a bioelectric network cannot be read out at the transcriptional or proteomic level and must be studied in living tissue.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Bioelectric network information cannot be read from transcript or protein levels";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Bioelectricity: the ancient cognitive glue”. Scope: Bioelectric networks of neural and non-neural cells"
}
